Hi all

I'm building a HMM-model to analyse survival rates of animals. The model works fine when fitted with commands nimbleMCMC or runMCMC (and associated calls), but when I try to perform k-fold-cross-validation using runCrossValidate, I get the following error:

"[Warning] Dynamic index out of bounds: dcat(prob = Psi[z[i, t_minus_1], 1:5])"

I thought this would be due to some problem with constants and/or initial values when splitting the data into folds. However, I couldn't figure it out.

I attached script with a reproducible example with a small fraction of the data.

Any help would he highly appreciated.

Thanks in advance,

-Antti

