> On Wednesday, March 22, 2023 at 9:47:42 AM UTC+11 Quresh Latif wrote:
> > In the user manual (0.4), the 'step' function is defined as returning 0 if x < 0, 1 if x > 0. I think what it returns when x = 0 is ambiguous, right? The JAGS user manual defines the step function as "Test for x >= 0". Since Nimble is for the most part written to be equivalent to JAGS, I am guessing step returns 1 when x = 0, but thought it would be worth confirming.
